From d63cf2b328fc3ccce1ebb9ce181dfd14af02734d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] playback mode notice: commas and a word, not middle dots and
 an arrow

The notice of the playback mode (videoscreen.hadesplaybackmode,
DescribePlaybackMode()) put a middle dot between its parts and an arrow
between the two formats of a conversion. It now writes the parts with
commas and the conversion with a word, as the public texts of the
project describe the notice: "Dolby Vision, FEL, 3840x2160 @ 23.976 Hz",
"Dolby Vision to HDR10". The mode keeps its "@", as the player
information writes it (ModeText()). The word is English, as the names
of the formats are: the notice has no string of its own for it.

The help of the setting gives the same examples (core 41102 and its
Estuary twin 32503, in en_gb and the three Spanish files, which quote
the notice as it is shown).

Host test: TestPlaybackMode with the new texts, and PlainCharacters,
which builds the text of every source, output, layers and mode (525
texts) and finds only printable ASCII in them. The new test fails on
the old header (5 of 9 tests), and the old test on the new one (4 of 8).
